1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
In this video we'll show you how to schedule scans in Burpsuite Enterprise Edition.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,600
Before we get started, just be aware that you can only create scans for sites that you've

3
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:21,920
already added to the system, so if you haven't created any sites yet please check out our

4
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:26,400
previous video for details on how to do this.

5
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:30,720
So once you've got your site set up, you've got a few different options for creating a

6
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:31,720
scan.

7
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:37,120
You can either drill down into the site and just click the new scan button, in which case

8
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,600
the site is pre-selected for you.

9
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:45,480
Alternatively, from anywhere in Burpsuite Enterprise Edition you can hover over the scans menu and

10
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:48,240
select create a new scan.

11
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:55,520
In this case you'll just need to select the site from the drop down menu.

12
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:59,640
So the first thing you need to decide is when you want your scan to start.

13
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:03,800
You can either schedule it to begin as soon as possible, or schedule it for a specific

14
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:05,080
time in the future.

15
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:09,260
For example, if you're scanning a site that other people are using to perform acceptance

16
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:14,360
testing you might want to schedule it to run overnight to avoid any impact on performance.

17
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:18,520
I'm going to schedule my scan to run at midnight.

18
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:27,080
Next, you can choose whether to create a one-off scan or create a recurring scan that repeats

19
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,960
on a regular basis.

20
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:32,360
I'll set my scan to run once per day.

21
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:39,000
By default, all recurring scans run indefinitely, but you can also specify a fixed number of repetitions,

22
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:46,440
or schedule the scan to run until a specific date.

23
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:50,800
Scan configurations give you really granular control over how Burps scan will behave, and

24
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:54,500
what sorts of issues it will check for.

25
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:58,740
There are plenty of built-in configurations for limiting the crawl time, restricting which

26
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:03,420
audit checks are performed, and generally just fine-tuning the scan to achieve better coverage

27
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:06,500
or speed, depending on what your priority is.

28
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:09,460
This can be really useful if you just want to get quick feedback, especially if you're

29
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:15,500
planning to incorporate the scan as part of a CI-CD workflow, for example.

30
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:19,480
If you're a Burpsuite professional user, you'll notice that most of the same built-in scan configurations

31
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:21,060
are available here.

32
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:24,360
You can also choose to create your own custom scan configurations, but we'll cover that in

33
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:26,520
a separate video.

34
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:30,880
It's worth pointing out at this stage that you don't actually have to select any scan configurations.

35
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:35,120
If you just leave this section blank, then Burpscanner will just use its default configuration, which

36
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:37,920
provides a good balance between coverage and speed.

37
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:41,940
You only need to add a configuration here if you want to override a particular setting or

38
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:45,120
group of settings.

39
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:49,000
If you click on the question mark next to each configuration, you can see exactly which setting

40
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,300
it overrides.

41
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:57,120
All of the options are grouped according to the kind of behaviour they control, so if a

42
00:02:57,120 --> 00:03:00,860
section's collapsed, like the login functions one here, this means that all of the settings

43
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:05,540
in that area are unchanged from Burpscanner's standard configuration.

44
00:03:05,540 --> 00:03:09,920
So as you can see here, applying this particular configuration hardly affects any of the settings,

45
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:14,540
but you will notice that the Crawl Limits section is expanded.

46
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:19,500
This shows us that one or more settings in this group are different from the standard configuration.

47
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:22,960
As you can probably tell from the name, applying this particular configuration just changes the

48
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:28,560
maximum crawl time to 30 minutes.

49
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:34,280
So going back to our scan, you probably noticed that a couple of scan configurations were already

50
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,700
pre-selected.

51
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:40,200
These are the default configurations that I specified when I created this site.

52
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:44,540
Whenever you're creating a new scan, you're free to override these defaults if you want to.

53
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:48,120
So this time I might want to run a slightly more thorough scan than usual, so I'll make a

54
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,120
couple of changes.

55
00:03:49,120 --> 00:04:04,220
I'll set the audit coverage thorough configuration and crawl strategy most complete.

56
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:08,040
As you can see, you can select multiple different configurations for the same scan, and these

57
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:12,700
are all applied in sequence, so you can combine several smaller configurations to create an overall

58
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:16,440
configuration that's tailored specifically for this particular site or for what you're trying

59
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:18,260
to achieve with this scan.

60
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:23,660
So now I'm happy with everything, I can go ahead and save.

61
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:26,220
As you can see, the scan's now scheduled.

62
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:29,460
Until it actually starts running, you've got the option to edit which scan configurations

63
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:36,880
are going to be applied, and you can also change the scheduling information if you want to.

64
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:42,900
If you choose to start your scan immediately, the scan status will indicate that it's waiting

65
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,900
for the next available agent.

66
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:48,220
Ideally, this should only take a few moments while the scan's initialised, but it does

67
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:52,120
depend on your licence and how many scans you already have running.

68
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:56,900
So if you've got a licence for 10 agents, for example, this means you can run up to 10 scans

69
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:57,720
at the same time.

70
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:01,840
Obviously, if you've already got 10 scans running, you'll have to wait until one of the

71
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:04,120
others has finished before this one can start.

72
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:08,440
This limitation also affects any scans that you've scheduled for a particular time of

73
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:11,940
day, so try to keep this in mind when you schedule new scans so that they don't all

74
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:13,940
coincide.

75
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:17,280
Remember that as your needs grow, you can add more agents to your licence at any time by

76
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:20,740
going to your account page on portswiger.net.

77
00:05:20,740 --> 00:05:23,820
And that's how you schedule a new scan in Berksuite Enterprise Edition.

